<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <article>
    <p class="eyebrow">48-Hour California Getaway</p>

    <h1>48 Hours in Paso Robles</h1>

    <p class="itinerary-subtitle">
      Two days of wine country, good food, and an easygoing downtown.
    </p>

    <img
      src="/images/paso-robles-vineyard-hero.jpg"
      alt="Vineyards stretching across the rolling hills of Paso Robles wine country"
      class="itinerary-hero"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p>
      Somewhere between California's coastal communities and the rolling
      hills of its inland wine country lies Paso Robles, a destination
      where a short getaway can feel considerably longer.
    </p>

    <p>
      Vineyards stretch across oak-covered hills, tasting rooms surround
      a walkable downtown, and some of the region's most rewarding
      experiences are close enough together that you don't have to
      spend your weekend racing from one stop to another.
    </p>

    <p>
      Whether you're visiting from elsewhere in California or including
      Paso Robles in a longer American road trip, two nights provide
      enough time to discover the area's character without feeling
      hurried.
    </p>

    <p>
      This itinerary isn't designed to show you everything Paso Robles
      has to offer. <strong>It's designed to help you have a really
      good two days there.</strong>
    </p>

    <nav class="itinerary-contents" aria-label="Itinerary contents">
      <p><strong>Plan Your Paso Robles Getaway</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#at-a-glance">At a Glance</a></li>
