    <h2 id="at-a-glance">At a Glance</h2>

    <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Wine lovers, couples, food-focused weekends, and relaxed getaways.</p>
    <p><strong>Ideal trip:</strong> Two nights / approximately 48 hours.</p>
    <p><strong>Home base:</strong> Downtown Paso Robles.</p>
    <p><strong>Getting around:</strong> Walk downtown; use a car with a designated driver or hired transportation for wine country.</p>
    <p><strong>Reserve ahead:</strong> Hotel, winery tastings, and weekend dinners.</p>
    <p><strong>Best pace:</strong> Two principal winery experiences in one day, with time to relax.</p>
    <p><strong>Have more time?</strong> Add Tin City for a few hours or Cambria and the coast for another day.</p>

    <h2 id="getting-there">Getting to Paso Robles</h2>

    <p>
      Paso Robles is located along US Highway 101 on California's
      Central Coast, making it a convenient stop between the
      San Francisco Bay Area and Southern California.
    </p>

    <h3>Arriving by Car</h3>

    <p>
      Allow approximately three to four hours from San Francisco
      or Los Angeles, depending on your starting point, traffic,
      and stops along the way.
    </p>

    <p>
      A car provides the greatest flexibility for exploring the
      surrounding countryside, although you can leave it parked
      for much of your time downtown.
    </p>

    <h3>Arriving by Air</h3>

    <p>
      San Luis Obispo County Regional Airport (SBP), approximately
      35 miles south of Paso Robles, is a convenient regional
      gateway.
    </p>

    <p>
      International visitors may find it easier to arrive through
      San Francisco or Los Angeles and include Paso Robles as
      part of a longer California road trip.
    </p>

    <h3>Arriving by Train</h3>

    <p>
      Amtrak's Coast Starlight serves Paso Robles, with its
      downtown station located at 800 Pine Street.
      Check current schedules and arrange transportation for
      any planned wine-country visits before arriving.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a href="https://www.amtrak.com/coast-starlight-train"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        Explore Amtrak's Coast Starlight
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2 id="where-to-stay">Where to Stay in Paso Robles</h2>

    <p>
      For this itinerary, staying close to downtown makes sense.
      You'll be able to leave the car behind for much of the first
      evening and again after returning from wine country.
    </p>

    <p class="affiliate-note">
      <strong>Affiliate disclosure:</strong> Some accommodation
      links below are affiliate links. We may earn a commission
      if you book through them, at no additional cost to you.
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Learn more.</a>
    </p>

